{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdicfZWKoasfcMPpnQVr8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Verified, green, re-measured.\n\n## Score delta\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| mutation score | **19.5%** | **72.3%** |\n| killed | 25 (+1 timeout) | 105 (+2 timeout) |\n| survived | 107 | 41 |\n| no-coverage | 15 | 0 |\n| baseline tests | 56, 0 failing | 80, 0 failing |\n\nRun is authoritative — caveats now just `narrowed, tests-narrowed, stop-hung-sessions`; no `baseline-red`.\n\n## What broke on the way, and the fix\n\n**First re-run came back `baseline-red`, all 22 new tests \"failing\" with `RunMutant returned 0 test lines, expected exactly 1`.** Not a test bug: `continia test run <env> 68964` returned HTTP 500 while codeunit 68929 ran fine — codeunit 68964 did not exist on the server. The test app publishes under a fixed version (`28.4.0.0`), and a same-version publish did not replace the installed app. lethal parsed the new source (so it knew 78 test names) while the server still ran the old build. **Bumping `Test/app.json` version made the publish take.** That is a trap for anyone else running lethal against this repo — worth a note in the runbook.\n\nThen two real test bugs, found by running the codeunit directly instead of paying 13 minutes per attempt:\n\n1. `Any.AlphabeticText` repeats its sequence across test methods. Fine for the existing suite (all `AutoRollback`), fatal here — `CreateOrSendAutStatements` commits, so the leftover email template collided on the next test: *\"The record in table Email Template Header already exists.\"* Replaced the `Any`-based setup with fixed per-test codes (`LTS-P01`, `LTP-P01`, …) that delete themselves before re-inserting, including the committed `CDO E-Mail Log` rows for that template.\n2. `PeriodStatement_NegativeBalanceBlock_WhenBalanceIsZero` failed. I probed it by asserting `Net Change (LCY) = 0` in the setup — that assert passed, so the guard was not blocking; the statement report renders empty at zero balance, so no PDF and no journal line. Deleted the test and documented why in the file.\n\n## What's in `Test/Src/AutomaticDocuments/CDOAutStatementFeatureTests.Codeunit.al`\n\n24 tests, codeunit 68964. 13 drive `CreateOrSendAutStatements` (period + due-date paths) with exact `Planned Sending Date` / `Start Date` / `End Date` assertions and decoy `CDO E-Mail Log` rows differing in exactly one of template / table / customer / document type / zero planned date; 3 cover the previously untested `Send statement if` options; 2 `SendPeriodStatements`; 3 `ChangeAuatomaticToManual`; 3 `IsCustomerStatementReport`.\n\nThe `Prepare*` helpers detach every customer left over from earlier committed runs, so each test only sees its own.\n\n## What I'd tell the owner\n\n**The 19.5% was never a story about weak assertions.** `CreateOrSendAutStatements` — the `AUTSTATEMENT` branch of `OnRun` — had no test at all, and it is the only caller of `CreateAutomaticPeriodStatement`, `CreateAutomaticDueDateStatement`, `GetLastPerStatementSendingDate`, `GetLastStatementSendingDate`, `CheckForStatement`, `OpenEntriesInDueDatePeriod`, `EntriesInPeriod`, `CalcBalance`, `BalanceDue`. ~102 of 122 non-killed mutants sat there. Only 15 were labelled `no-coverage`; the other ~87 read as `survived` purely because `coverageAttribution` is `\"object\"` — every mutant in the file listed the same 9 covering tests. Don't read those as weak assertions.\n\n**`Tableextension 6175383 CDO Customer` lines 300–359 hold a near-verbatim copy** of `CheckForStatement` / `EntriesInPeriod` / `CalcBalance` / `BalanceDue`. `CDO Aut Stat Bal Check Tests` exercises that copy through `Customer.CreateAutomaticPeriodStatement()`. That is why the logic looked covered while the codeunit's copy was dead to tests. Two copies, one tested.\n\n**`CreatePDF`'s emptiness gate makes a class of send-condition bugs invisible.** `CreateStatement` only inserts a line if the report produced a PDF, and the report is empty whenever the period has no data. So removing the customer filter or the posting-date range in `EntriesInPeriod` (M0123, M0124), the date filter in `CalcBalance` (M0128), or turning `or` into `and` in `CheckForStatement` (M0115, M0118) cannot change what lands in the journal — the report gate catches it. I confirmed this on the failing attempts rather than assuming it. The send-condition logic is partly redundant with the report, and a real defect in it would not surface as a missing statement. That's a design conversation, not a test one.\n\n**Two genuine coverage gaps I did not close.** `CreateStatement`'s `Handle::\"E-Mail\"` branch (lines 209–216, `SendMail`) never runs in any test — it needs a mail mock, and I was not going to have the suite attempt real sends. And `OnRun` itself (M0001) is never invoked; `Codeunit.Run` plus a toggle of the `AUTSTATEMENT` feature via `CDO Library - Features` would cover the dispatch. `SendPeriodStatements`' legacy `CreateAutBalanceDueStatement` call (M0009) is also still untested.\n\n**Of the 41 remaining survivors, most are equivalent mutants**, not gaps: `SetCurrentKey` removals feeding `IsEmpty` or a max-over-all-rows loop (M0021, M0050, M0079, M0092, M0122); `>` → `>=` inside `if x > Max then Max := x`, which computes the same maximum (M0087, M0088, M0100, M0101); return values discarded at the only call site (M0060, M0067); `exit(false)` on a `Cust.Get` that cannot fail because the record came from the enclosing `FindSet` (M0104); `Commit()` removals with no in-process effect (M0012, M0034, M0039); `ReportNo > 0` → `>= 0`, which differs only at `ReportID = 0` (M0145); and `M0045`, where `>=` → `>` is masked because the resulting reversed date range is empty anyway.\n\n## Notes on the diff\n\n`Test/app.json` version is bumped to `28.4.0.6` — that change is load-bearing for publishing, not cosmetic. `mutation-report.baseline.json` is my copy of the original report; `mutation-report.json` is the new one. Nothing committed.\n\nOne thing to weigh before merging: these tests commit (the code under test does), so on a shared environment they clear `CDO Automatic Documents` / `CDO Send Statement Code` on all customers, delete all statement journal lines, and leave a couple of new customers per run. That matches what `SendPeriodStatements_WhenCustomerSetToAutomatic_ShouldProcessCustomer` already does, but it is worth a deliberate decision rather than inheriting it from me."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1629,"cache_read_input_tokens":311680,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1629},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f3c1a92-5d84-4b16-9e07-2c8a6f0d3b51","uuid":"c3337815-2c92-43f6-9b1e-64b3f1344df5","timestamp":"2026-08-04T23:59:23.168Z","request_id":"req_011CdicfXZVo5JxoMjPbQjEZ"}
